(g)
facilities to be given by the lessee for working other minerals in the leased area or adjacent area;
(h)
the entering and working in a reserved or protected forest;
(i)
the securing of pits and shafts;
(j)
the reporting of accidents;
(k)
indemnity to Government against the claim of a third party for any damage, injury or disturbance caused to him by the
lessee;
(l)
the delivery of possession of lands and mines on the surrender, expiration or termination of the lease;
(m)
the time limit for removal of mineral, ore, plant, machinery and other properties from the lease hold area after expiration,
